  "ranking": "Eight symmetric configurations (same recipe in both independent banks; not all64 asymmetric pairs), sustained uniform OD mixtures at the daily model's mean rates. Discard first600s; score next1200s arrivals. S6 scored for7200s to avoid sparse empty windows. Rank equal-day development AWT, tie by configuration name; freeze top2. These are finite-candidate episode rankings, not true universal optima.",
  "fixed": "Re-evaluate all8 on complete development days; select fixed by load and global equal-load/equal-seed champion. No old empirical result data reused.",
  "transitions": "At12 representative clock boundaries of each development day under load's frozen fixed champion AND naive clock champion switching, deepcopy identical full state. Keep and change one bank at a time to each of target regime's top2 sustained candidates. Other bank holds incumbent. Truncate future arrivals at boundary+900s, then drain. Score remaining waits of physically waiting plus future arrivals (onboard excluded); an empty transition cohort has explicitly flagged zero waiting opportunity, not an estimated passenger mean. No warm-start reset or future-leaking policy.",
  "gate": "Group development paired switch-minus-keep by load,target regime,incumbent, bank-local bin(clear/occupied/busy). Average banks/boundaries within seed first. Require >=3 seed replicates, mean<=-.5s, upper simultaneous95% CI<0 across all tested development cells/actions, p90ratio<=1.05 and LWTincrease<=1pp. Choose lowest mean eligible action, otherwise retain. Bins: clear=no latches or riders; busy=at least3 latches or16 onboard; occupied=other.",
  "daily": "Compare frozen fixed_level,fixed_global,naive regime champions,gated local rule on unseen full24h days. Gated checks only at regime changes, per-bank local observations, retaining when unsupported. No anticipatory parking/lead tuning.",
  "heldout_transitions": "From independent heldout fixed-policy snapshots compare keep, both-bank naive champion and simultaneous independent local gate. Recreate snapshots separately at both resolutions.",
